summary: Upload the artifact-server qcow2 to AWS as an AMI

description: |
    Import the upstream testing-farm/tests ``/testing-farm/upload-qcow2/aws`` plan
    (https://gitlab.com/testing-farm/tests/-/tree/main/testing-farm/upload-qcow2),
    which uploads a qcow2 to AWS with ``tft-admin`` inside the cnc image, and
    copies it to us-east-2.

    The Makefile derives QCOW2_URL from the qcow2 build request with
    ``qcow2-url.py`` before it submits this plan.

    Required variables:

      QCOW2_URL         ... Download URL of the qcow2.

      IMAGE_NAME        ... Image name under which it is stored in the cloud.

      QCOW2_ARCH        ... Arch of the qcow2, passed to tft-admin.

    Optional variables:

      REMOVE_AFTER_TEST ... When set, delete the uploaded image after the upload.

    Secret variables:

      VAULT_SECRET_ID   ... Hashicorp Vault secret id for the cnc container. Pass as a
                            Testing Farm secret (``-s``).

plan:
  import:
    url: https://gitlab.com/testing-farm/tests
    ref: main
    name: /testing-farm/upload-qcow2/aws
